  "body": "### Checks\n\n- [x] I have updated to the lastest minor and patch version of Strands\n- [x] I have checked the documentation and this is not expected behavior\n- [x] I have searched [./issues](./issues?q=) and there are no duplicates of my issue\n\n### SDK Language\n\nPython\n\n### Strands Version\n\n1.50.2\n\n### Language Runtime Version\n\nPython 3.12\n\n### Operating System\n\nAmazon Linux 2 (EC2)\n\n### Installation Method\n\npip\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Deploy to an EC2 instance without `AWS_DEFAULT_REGION` or `AWS_REGION` environment variables set\n2. Instantiate a `BedrockKnowledgeBaseStore`, wrap in try-except if you want to actually catch the error:\n\n```python\nfrom strands.vended_memory_stores import BedrockKnowledgeBaseStore\n\nstore = BedrockKnowledgeBaseStore(\n    name=\"user-memory\",\n    description=\"Personal memories about the user\",\n    scope=\"user-123\",\n    writable=True,\n    config={\n        \"knowledge_base_id\": \"ABCDEFGHIJ\",\n        \"data_source_type\": \"S3\",\n        \"data_source_id\": \"DATASOURCE123\",\n        \"s3\": {\n            \"bucket\": \"my-bucket\",\n            \"prefix\": \"memories/\",\n        },\n    },\n)\n```\n\n3. Observe error:\n\n```\nNoRegionError: You must specify a region.\n```\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nThe `BedrockKnowledgeBaseStore` constructor or its `config` dict should accept a `region` or `region_name` parameter to specify the AWS region, similar to how `BedrockModel` accepts `region_name`, or just pick it up from the IAM role associated with the cloud resource (in this case EC2 but could be Lambda, etc.):\n\n```python\n# This works for BedrockModel:\nmodel = BedrockModel(model_id=\"anthropic.claude-3-sonnet\", region_name=\"us-west-2\")\n\n# Expected for BedrockKnowledgeBaseStore:\nstore = BedrockKnowledgeBaseStore(\n    name=\"user-memory\",\n    ...,\n    config={\n        \"knowledge_base_id\": \"ABCDEFGHIJ\",\n        \"region\": \"us-west-2\",  # or region_name\n        ...\n    },\n)\n```\n\n## Additional Context\n\nThe error originates from boto3 client initialization inside the store. The `BedrockModel` class properly exposes `region_name` as a parameter, but `BedrockKnowledgeBaseStore` does not appear to pass region configuration to its internal boto3 clients.\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nDefaults to some region or another or respects IAM role region and permissions on the deployed EC2 or cloud resource.\n\n### Actual Behavior\n\nSeems to work fine on local `aws sso login` and pulls those regions fine. Does not operate the same way in Cloud env.\n\n### Additional Context\n\n_No response_\n\n### Possible Solution\n\n_No response_\n\n### Related Issues\n\n_No response_",
